properties.Language Requirements:
Erasmus School of History, Culture and Communication(ESHCC) 혹은 Erasmus University College(EUC)로 신청할 수 있으며, 각각 지원자격 및 수강가능 과목범위가 다를 수 있으니 반드시 파견교 웹사이트 및 팩트시트를 통해 확인하시기 바랍니다. 
* EUC : https://www.eur.nl/en/euc/education/exchange/incoming-students#exchange-admission-application
   - TOEFL (internet based version): a total score of at least 100 points, with scores of at least 20 points for each sub topic;
   - IELTS (academic version): a total score of at least 7.0, with scores of at least 6.0 for each sub topic;

properties.Restrictions:
* GPA At least 2.75 out of a 4.0 scale
* Course availability: exchange students may take courses across departments, except for the ones offered by the following departments:
- International Master’s Program in Asia-Pacific Studies (IMAS);
- International Master of Business Administration (IMBA);
- Executive Master of Business Administration (EMBA);
- College of Global Banking and Finance;
- On-Job Training Programs;
- Extended Minor Course with credit fee; and
- The department of the students’ native language (e.g., Korean students cannot take courses offered by the Department of Korean Language and Culture). 
* For doctoral students, the choice for English-taught courses is quite limited. Please see the course list before considering the exchange program.
